    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d703-a1">

                <pb facs="0925" n="813" sameAs="frus:frus1918/pg813"/>

                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Mexico</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Fletcher</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1918-11-22T20:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">November 22, 1918, 8 p.m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1656. Your 1710, November 15. Press Mexican Government for consideration of your
                    communications, and endeavor to obtain favorable reply in near future. Claims
                    against Mexico are being revived with forceful insistence, and Department deems
                    it very important that it should be in position to state that some progress has
                    been made in the organization of a commission to which American claimants can be
                    referred.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Lansing</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
